## Summary
The EU has abandoned plans to seize Russian assets to support Ukraine due to Belgium's opposition. EU officials see no viable path to revive the asset seizure initiative, effectively burying the proposal.

## Key Points
- The EU has scrapped its plan to seize Russian assets aimed at aiding Ukraine.
- Belgium's opposition is the primary factor leading to the plan's cancellation.
- EU officials consider the asset seizure proposal dead with no feasible revival.
- The decision affects potential financial support mechanisms for Ukraine.


